                     MAILER General User Commands

               (c) Copyright Princeton Univeristy, 1990.

  The VM Network Mailer is a mail transport agent.  That is, it is a
  program that decides how to route properly formatted mail messages
  through the network.  Mailer spends most of its time reading files
  that have been sent to it from local and remote users on the network
  and deciding if there are local or remote recipients to whom the
  file should be sent.

  In addition to processing mail files it will respond to a small set
  of commands.  These commands may be issued from the Mailer's console
  or by sending them using the CP SMSG, the CP MSG or the CMS TELL
  command.

 The syntax specification of Mailer general user commands follows.
 Changes since the last version of this file are flagged with a '|'
 (vertical bar) in column 1.

  +--------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                                                                    |
  |  FORWARD - Deliver mail to a userid other than the one specified   |
  |            in the headers.  It is legal to forward mail to more    |
  |            than 1 address.  If you want to continue to receive     |
  |            a copy of the mail at your userid, add a forward with   |
  |            an address of '<*>'.                                    |
  |                                                                    |
  |      FORWARD ADD    destaddr                                       |
  |              DELETE destaddr | ALL                                 |
  |              LIST                                                  |
  |                                                                    |
  |  HELP | ? - Get list of commands.                                  |
  |                                                                    |
  |  SHOW <show-options>  - Display assorted counters, etc.            |
  |                                                                    |
  |  show-options:                                                     |
  |                                                                    |
| |    BIT  bitname|*                                                  |
| |     Display the current setting of Mailer bit flags.  These values |
| |     are normally set from the Mailer profile.                      |
  |                                                                    |
  |    STATUS                                                          |
  |     Various Mailer status variables are returned.  These are:      |
  |     Since: <date time> - time of last Mailer restart.              |
  |     Msgs in/out: Number of messages (mail) received and sent.      |
  |     Max Multi:  Maximum number of recipients for a single message. |
  |     Stack Max:  Percentage Mailer internal storage utilization.    |
  |                                                                    |
  |    DOMAINS <domain-name>                                           |
  |     Statistics on outgoing files to other domain Mailers.          |
  |                                                                    |
  |    INCOMING <nodename> <userid>                                    |
  |     Statistics on files received from other network Mailers.       |
  |                                                                    |
  |    OUTGOING <hostname>                                             |
  |     Statistics on outgoing files to other network Mailers.         |
  |                                                                    |
| |    PATH hostname | domain-name                                     |
| |     Displays how Mailer would deliver mail having this hostname    |
| |     or domain-name as its destination.                             |
  |                                                                    |
  |    SPECIAL <userid>                                                |
  |     Statistics on mail to special userids (i.e. SYSTEM).           |
  |                                                                    |
| |    VERSION                                                         |
| |     Returns information about the release level of the mailer.     |
  |                                                                    |
  |  SMSG - Used as a prefix to other commands causes the reply to     |
| |         be sent as a machine-readable SMSG.  SMSG is not sensible  |
| |         from the Mailer console.                                   |
  |                                                                    |
  +--------------------------------------------------------------------+

| Sample commands:
|
| To find out the release level of a mailer at the local node
|
|    TELL mailerid SHOW VERSION
|
| To find out the release level of a mailer at a remote VM node
|
|    TELL mailerid AT node SHOW VERSION
